  "description": "Cornelia, who married the aged Marquis Meitner at a young age and became a Marchioness, seemed to have gained freedom with the Marquis's death, but faced with the prospect of relinquishing her title and becoming penniless due to the absence of an heir, hatches a plan to seduce three attractive men who visit her husband's funeral. Isaac, a naive commoner who studied medicine; Richard, a profligate poet who warms the bedrooms of noblewomen with his eloquence and courtesan skills; and Theodore, a conquest-hungry Duke bent on conquering Cornelia.\n\n *\"I've endured ten years, and now I'm in the arms of another old man?\"\n\"Duke Theodore is a young duke. And—his breasts are bigger than yours.\"\n\"You should have said that first.\"* \n\nAs they get to know Cornelia, the three men find themselves helplessly drawn to her honest yet cheeky demeanor. But who will remain by her side until the very end?\n\n(Source: Lezhin, translated)",
